{
  "_what_this_is": "Every move of a file under docs/ into the place its class gives it (docs/documentation_process.md, \"Where documents live\"; the owner, 20 November 2026: \"can you please start an agent to improve the organization of the docs directory? it's become insanely bloated\"). `moves` are made: the file was renamed on `date` with its name unchanged, and the references that must name the new path were changed in the same commit. Records, the decision log, the frozen baseline and the provenance columns of tables still write the old path, as they were written, and this list (printed in docs/file_index.md) is how a reader finds the file from it. `planned` moves are not made yet: phase 2 waits for work in flight on another branch or in another checkout that changes a file the move must edit, and phase 3 holds the build inputs, moved just before a data-layer rebuild. What a planned move waits for is recomputed on the day by the rule, not stored here.",
  "_how_it_is_used": "experiments/move_documents.py --phase N applies a phase (a dry run without --apply) and moves its entries from `planned` to `moves`; tests/test_documentation_process.py checks that every move is made, every planned source is still in place, every document not planned sits where its class puts it, and no code or YAML config names a moved path.",
